<procedure name="gen_arrow_contour_xld">
<interface>
<oo>
<par name="Arrow" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</oo>
<ic>
<par name="Row1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Column1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Row2" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Column2" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="HeadLength" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="HeadWidth" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
</interface>
<body>
<c>* This procedure generates arrow shaped XLD contours,</c>
<c>* pointing from (Row1, Column1) to (Row2, Column2).</c>
<c>* If starting and end point are identical, a contour consisting</c>
<c>* of a single point is returned.</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* input parameteres:</c>
<c>* Row1, Column1: Coordinates of the arrows' starting points</c>
<c>* Row2, Column2: Coordinates of the arrows' end points</c>
<c>* HeadLength, HeadWidth: Size of the arrow heads in pixels</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* output parameter:</c>
<c>* Arrow: The resulting XLD contour</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* The input tuples Row1, Column1, Row2, and Column2 have to be of</c>
<c>* the same length.</c>
<c>* HeadLength and HeadWidth either have to be of the same length as</c>
<c>* Row1, Column1, Row2, and Column2 or have to be a single element.</c>
<c>* If one of the above restrictions is violated, an error will occur.</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Init</c>
<l>gen_empty_obj (Arrow)</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Calculate the arrow length</c>
<l>distance_pp (Row1, Column1, Row2, Column2, Length)</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Mark arrows with identical start and end point</c>
<c>* (set Length to -1 to avoid division-by-zero exception)</c>
<l>ZeroLengthIndices := find(Length,0)</l>
<l>if (ZeroLengthIndices != -1)</l>
<l>    Length[ZeroLengthIndices] := -1</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Calculate auxiliary variables.</c>
<l>DR := 1.0 * (Row2 - Row1) / Length</l>
<l>DC := 1.0 * (Column2 - Column1) / Length</l>
<l>HalfHeadWidth := HeadWidth / 2.0</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Calculate end points of the arrow head.</c>
<l>RowP1 := Row1 + (Length - HeadLength) * DR + HalfHeadWidth * DC</l>
<l>ColP1 := Column1 + (Length - HeadLength) * DC - HalfHeadWidth * DR</l>
<l>RowP2 := Row1 + (Length - HeadLength) * DR - HalfHeadWidth * DC</l>
<l>ColP2 := Column1 + (Length - HeadLength) * DC + HalfHeadWidth * DR</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Finally create output XLD contour for each input point pair</c>
<l>for Index := 0 to |Length| - 1 by 1</l>
<l>    if (Length[Index] == -1)</l>
<c>        * Create_ single points for arrows with identical start and end point</c>
<l>        gen_contour_polygon_xld (TempArrow, Row1[Index], Column1[Index])</l>
<l>    else</l>
<c>        * Create arrow contour</c>
<l>        gen_contour_polygon_xld (TempArrow, [Row1[Index],Row2[Index],RowP1[Index],Row2[Index],RowP2[Index],Row2[Index]], [Column1[Index],Column2[Index],ColP1[Index],Column2[Index],ColP2[Index],Column2[Index]])</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>    concat_obj (Arrow, TempArrow, Arrow)</l>
<l>endfor</l>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="gen_arrow_contour_xld">
<abstract lang="en_US">This procedure creates arrow shaped XLD contours, which point from the coordinates (Row1, Column1) to the coordinates (Row2, Coordinates2). The shape of the arrow head can be specified with the parameters HeadLength and HeadWidth (in pixels).

If starting and end point are identical, a contour consisting of a single point is returned.

The input tuples Row1, Column1, Row2, and Column2 have to be of the same length. HeadLength and HeadWidth either have to be of the same length as Row1, Column1, Row2, and Column2 or have to be a single element. If one of the above restrictions is violated, an error will occur.
</abstract>
<alternatives>
<item>disp_arrow</item>
<item>gen_contour_polygon_xld</item>
</alternatives>
<chapters lang="de_DE">
<item>XLD</item>
<item>Generierung</item>
</chapters>
<chapters lang="en_US">
<item>XLD</item>
<item>Creation</item>
</chapters>
<example lang="en_US">StartPointRows:=[100,100]
StartPointColumns:=[100,100]
EndPointRows:=[200,50]
EndPointColumns:=[200,150]
dev_set_colored (3)
gen_arrow_contour_xld (Arrow, StartPointRows, StartPointColumns, EndPointRows, EndPointColumns, [10,20], [20,10])
</example>
<keywords lang="de_DE">
<item>XLD-Konturen erzeugen</item>
<item>XLD-Kontur eines Pfeils erzeugen</item>
</keywords>
<keywords lang="en_US">
<item>create XLD contours</item>
<item>create XLD contour of arrow</item>
</keywords>
<library lang="de_DE">MVTec Standard Procedures</library>
<library lang="en_US">MVTec Standard Procedures</library>
<see_also>
<item>gen_contour_nurbs_xld</item>
</see_also>
<short lang="de_DE">Creates an arrow shaped XLD contour.</short>
<short lang="en_US">Creates an arrow shaped XLD contour.</short>
<successor>
<item>dev_display</item>
<item>disp_obj</item>
</successor>
<parameters>
<parameter id="Arrow">
<description lang="en_US">The generated xld</description>
<multivalue>optional</multivalue>
<sem_type>xld_cont</sem_type>
</parameter>
<parameter id="Column1">
<default_type>integer</default_type>
<default_value>100</default_value>
<description lang="en_US">The column coordinate of the starting point</description>
<mixed_type>optional</mixed_type>
<multivalue>optional</multivalue>
<sem_type>point.x</sem_type>
<type_list>
<item>integer</item>
<item>real</item>
</type_list>
</parameter>
<parameter id="Column2">
<default_type>integer</default_type>
<default_value>200</default_value>
<description lang="en_US">The column coordinate of the end point</description>
<mixed_type>optional</mixed_type>
<multivalue>optional</multivalue>
<sem_type>point.x</sem_type>
<type_list>
<item>integer</item>
<item>real</item>
</type_list>
</parameter>
<parameter id="HeadLength">
<default_type>integer</default_type>
<default_value>5</default_value>
<description lang="en_US">The length of the arrow head in pixels</description>
<mixed_type>optional</mixed_type>
<multivalue>optional</multivalue>
<sem_type>number</sem_type>
<type_list>
<item>integer</item>
<item>real</item>
</type_list>
<values>
<item>[2,3,5,10,20]</item>
</values>
</parameter>
<parameter id="HeadWidth">
<default_type>integer</default_type>
<default_value>5</default_value>
<description lang="en_US">The width of the arrow head in pixels</description>
<mixed_type>optional</mixed_type>
<multivalue>optional</multivalue>
<sem_type>number</sem_type>
<type_list>
<item>integer</item>
<item>real</item>
</type_list>
<values>
<item>[2,3,5,10,20]</item>
</values>
</parameter>
<parameter id="Row1">
<default_type>integer</default_type>
<default_value>100</default_value>
<description lang="en_US">The row coordinate of the starting point</description>
<mixed_type>optional</mixed_type>
<multivalue>optional</multivalue>
<sem_type>point.y</sem_type>
<type_list>
<item>integer</item>
<item>real</item>
</type_list>
</parameter>
<parameter id="Row2">
<default_type>integer</default_type>
<default_value>200</default_value>
<description lang="en_US">The row coordinate of the end point</description>
<mixed_type>optional</mixed_type>
<multivalue>optional</multivalue>
<sem_type>point.y</sem_type>
<type_list>
<item>integer</item>
<item>real</item>
</type_list>
</parameter>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="DisplayImageAndRegions_Local">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="ImageOrig" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RinnenROIs" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="EjectROIs" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</io>
<ic>
<par name="DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
</interface>
<body>
<l>get_image_size (ImageOrig, ImageOrig_Width, ImageOrig_Height)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>if (DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1 = 0)</l>
<l>    dev_set_window (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>    dev_set_part (0, 0, ImageOrig_Height, ImageOrig_Width)</l>
<l>    dev_display (ImageOrig)</l>
<l>    dev_set_color ('blue')</l>
<l>    dev_display (RinnenROIs)</l>
<l>    dev_set_color ('gray')</l>
<l>    dev_display (EjectROIs)</l>
<l>else</l>
<l>    set_part (WindowHandle, 0, 0, ImageOrig_Height, ImageOrig_Width)</l>
<l>    disp_obj (ImageOrig, WindowHandle)</l>
<l>    set_color (WindowHandle, 'blue')</l>
<l>    disp_region (RinnenROIs, WindowHandle)</l>
<l>    set_color (WindowHandle, 'gray')</l>
<l>    disp_region (EjectROIs, WindowHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="DisplayImageAndRegions_Local">
<parameters>
<parameter id="DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1"/>
<parameter id="EjectROIs"/>
<parameter id="ImageOrig"/>
<parameter id="RinnenROIs"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="Display_EjectMovementCompensationLines">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="EjectROIs" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</io>
<ic>
<par name="DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Shiftregister_EjectPositionMovementCompensationVector" base_type="ctrl" dimension="2"/>
</ic>
</interface>
<body>
<l>smallest_rectangle1 (EjectROIs, Row1, Column1, Row2, Column2)</l>
<l>convert_vector_to_tuple (Shiftregister_EjectPositionMovementCompensationVector, EjectCompensationValues)</l>
<l>tuple_length (EjectCompensationValues, EjectCompensationValues_Length)</l>
<l>tuple_select_range (Row1, 0, EjectCompensationValues_Length-1, Row1)</l>
<l>tuple_select_range (Row2, 0, EjectCompensationValues_Length-1, Row2)</l>
<l>tuple_select_range (Column1, 0, EjectCompensationValues_Length-1, Column1)</l>
<l>tuple_select_range (Column2, 0, EjectCompensationValues_Length-1, Column2)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>gen_rectangle1 (CompensationRectangle, Row1-EjectCompensationValues, Column1, Row2, Column2)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>if (DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1 = 0)</l>
<l>    dev_set_color ('red')</l>
<l>    dev_display (CompensationRectangle)</l>
<l>else</l>
<l>    set_color (WindowHandle, 'red')</l>
<l>    disp_obj (CompensationRectangle, WindowHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="Display_EjectMovementCompensationLines">
<parameters>
<parameter id="DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1"/>
<parameter id="EjectROIs"/>
<parameter id="Shiftregister_EjectPositionMovementCompensationVector"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="VisualisationOfObjectRegions">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="ImageOrig" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RinnenROIs" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="EjectROIs" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="GoodObjectVector_TabletIndividual_WidthGood_ThreadVector" base_type="iconic" dimension="3"/>
<par name="ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area_ThreadVector" base_type="iconic" dimension="3"/>
</io>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine_Vector" base_type="ctrl" dimension="1"/>
<par name="DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Shiftregister_EjectPositionMovementCompensationVector" base_type="ctrl" dimension="2"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="Time_Needed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<l>* convert_vector_to_tuple (Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine_Vector, Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine)</l>
<l>count_seconds (Seconds_Start)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>* DisplayImageAndRegions_Local (ImageOrig, RinnenROIs, EjectROIs, DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1, WindowHandle)</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<l>* stop ()</l>
<l>* dev_display (ImageOrig)</l>
<c></c>
<c>* Visu of good and bad objects</c>
<l>gen_empty_obj (ErrorObject_Colour)</l>
<l>gen_empty_obj (ErrorObject_Width)</l>
<l>gen_empty_obj (ErrorObject_Diameter)</l>
<l>gen_empty_obj (ErrorObject_Spots)</l>
<l>gen_empty_obj (ErrorObject_Area)</l>
<l>gen_empty_obj (TabletIndividual)</l>
<l>gen_empty_obj (GoodObject_Width)</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Have two loops for object reconstruction. The outer one loops through the processes data, the inner one through the lanes data</c>
<l>ThreadingVectorLength := ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area_ThreadVector.length()</l>
<l>for VectorIndex := 0 to ThreadingVectorLength-1 by 1</l>
<l>    ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area := ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area_ThreadVector.at(VectorIndex)</l>
<l>    GoodObjectVector_TabletIndividual_WidthGood := GoodObjectVector_TabletIndividual_WidthGood_ThreadVector.at(VectorIndex)</l>
<c>    * inner loop throug lanes data</c>
<l>    LanesVectorLength := ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area_ThreadVector.at(VectorIndex).length()</l>
<l>    for Index := 0 to LanesVectorLength-1 by 1</l>
<l>        concat_obj (ErrorObject_Colour, ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area.at(Index).at(0), ErrorObject_Colour)</l>
<c>        * have a boxlike visualisation for leght errors</c>
<l>        concat_obj (ErrorObject_Width, ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area.at(Index).at(1), ErrorObject_Width)</l>
<l>        concat_obj (ErrorObject_Diameter, ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area.at(Index).at(2), ErrorObject_Diameter)</l>
<l>        concat_obj (ErrorObject_Spots, ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area.at(Index).at(3), ErrorObject_Spots)</l>
<l>        concat_obj (ErrorObject_Area, ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area.at(Index).at(4), ErrorObject_Area)</l>
<l>        concat_obj (TabletIndividual, GoodObjectVector_TabletIndividual_WidthGood.at(Index).at(0), TabletIndividual)</l>
<l>        concat_obj (GoodObject_Width, GoodObjectVector_TabletIndividual_WidthGood.at(Index).at(1), GoodObject_Width)</l>
<l>    endfor</l>
<l>endfor</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>* stop ()</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<l>select_shape (TabletIndividual, SelectedRegions, 'area', 'and', 1, 9999999999)</l>
<l>dev_display (SelectedRegions)</l>
<c></c>
<l>* concat_obj (ErrorObject_Colour, ErrorObject_Width, ErrorObjectsConcat)</l>
<l>* concat_obj (ErrorObjectsConcat, ErrorObject_Diameter, ErrorObjectsConcat)</l>
<l>* concat_obj (ErrorObjectsConcat, ErrorObject_Spots, ErrorObjectsConcat)</l>
<l>* concat_obj (ErrorObjectsConcat, ErrorObject_Area, ErrorObjectsConcat)</l>
<l>* select_shape (ErrorObjectsConcat, ErrorObjectsConcat, 'area', 'and', 1, 9999999999)</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* only display if objects are avalable- speeds up process</c>
<c>* </c>
<l>* count_obj (GoodObject_Width, Number)</l>
<l>* if (Number # 0)</l>
<l>*     if (DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1 = 0)</l>
<l>*         dev_set_color ('green')</l>
<l>*         dev_display (GoodObject_Width)</l>
<l>*     else</l>
<l>*         set_color (WindowHandle, 'green')</l>
<l>*         disp_region (GoodObject_Width, WindowHandle)</l>
<l>*     endif</l>
<l>* endif</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>* stop ()</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<l>* count_obj (ErrorObjectsConcat, Number)</l>
<l>* if (Number # 0)</l>
<l>* if (DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1 = 0)</l>
<l>*     dev_set_color ('red')</l>
<l>*     dev_display (ErrorObjectsConcat)</l>
<l>* else</l>
<l>*     set_color (WindowHandle, 'red')</l>
<l>*     disp_region (ErrorObjectsConcat, WindowHandle)</l>
<l>* endif</l>
<l>* endif</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<l>* stop ()</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>* ShiftregisterVectorLength := Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine_Vector.length()</l>
<c>* the offset is necessary for working with mutiple threadresults</c>
<l>* Eject_ROI_Offset := 0</l>
<l>* for VectorIndex := 0 to ShiftregisterVectorLength-1 by 1</l>
<l>* Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine := Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine_Vector.at(VectorIndex)</l>
<l>* tuple_greater_elem (Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine, 1, Greater)</l>
<l>* tuple_sum (Greater, NumberToSelect)</l>
<l>* tuple_sort_index (-Greater, Indices_ToSelect)</l>
<l>* if (NumberToSelect&gt;=1)</l>
<l>* tuple_select_range (Indices_ToSelect, 0, NumberToSelect-1, Selected)</l>
<l>* select_obj (EjectROIs, ObjectsSelected, Selected+Eject_ROI_Offset+1)</l>
<l>* if (DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1 = 0)</l>
<l>*     dev_set_color ('red')</l>
<l>*     dev_display (ObjectsSelected)</l>
<l>* else</l>
<l>*     set_color (WindowHandle, 'red')</l>
<l>*     disp_obj (ObjectsSelected, WindowHandle)</l>
<l>* endif</l>
<c>* first get the boxes with active eject</c>
<l>* tuple_add (Selected, 1, Selected)</l>
<c>* write the number of ejects to it</c>
<l>* for Index := 0 to NumberToSelect-1 by 1</l>
<l>* select_obj (ObjectsSelected, SingleBox, Index+1)</l>
<l>* area_center (SingleBox, _, Row, Column)</l>
<l>* set_tposition (WindowHandle, Row-14, Column-14)</l>
<l>* SelectedEjectNumberElement := Selected[Index]</l>
<l>* NumberErrorsInEjectBox := Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine[SelectedEjectNumberElement]</l>
<l>* write_string (WindowHandle, NumberErrorsInEjectBox)</l>
<l>* endfor</l>
<l>* endif</l>
<l>* tuple_length (Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine, Offset_Temp)</l>
<l>* Eject_ROI_Offset := Eject_ROI_Offset + Offset_Temp</l>
<l>* endfor</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>* Display_EjectMovementCompensationLines (EjectROIs, DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1, WindowHandle, Shiftregister_EjectPositionMovementCompensationVector)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>count_seconds (Seconds_End)</l>
<l>Time_Needed := (Seconds_End - Seconds_Start)*1000</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="VisualisationOfObjectRegions">
<parameters>
<parameter id="DevWindow0_NonDevWindow1"/>
<parameter id="EjectROIs"/>
<parameter id="ErrorObjectVector_Colour_Width_Diameter_Spots_Area_ThreadVector"/>
<parameter id="GoodObjectVector_TabletIndividual_WidthGood_ThreadVector"/>
<parameter id="ImageOrig"/>
<parameter id="RinnenROIs"/>
<parameter id="Shiftregister_EjectFoundPerLine_Vector"/>
<parameter id="Shiftregister_EjectPositionMovementCompensationVector"/>
<parameter id="Time_Needed"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="ButtonsIntervaceViaFile">
<interface>
<ic>
<par name="FilenameIntervaceFile" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn0FlagTeachInSuccessfull" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn2" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn3" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn4" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn5IconArrowLeft" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn6IconArrowRight" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn7CancelDraw" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn8ProgressBar" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Btn9HelpText" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="BtnACaption" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="BtnB" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="BtnC" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="BtnD" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
</interface>
<body>
<l>* set_system ('filename_encoding', 'utf8')</l>
<l>open_file (FilenameIntervaceFile, 'output', FileHandle)</l>
<l>if (Btn0FlagTeachInSuccessfull # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '0;' + Btn0FlagTeachInSuccessfull)</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn1 # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '1;' + Btn1)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn2 # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '2;' + Btn2)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn3 # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '3;' + Btn3)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn4 # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '4;' + Btn4)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn5IconArrowLeft # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '5;' + Btn5IconArrowLeft)</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn6IconArrowRight # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '6;' + Btn6IconArrowRight)</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn7CancelDraw # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '7;' + Btn7CancelDraw)</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn8ProgressBar # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '8;' + Btn8ProgressBar)</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (Btn9HelpText # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, '9;' + Btn9HelpText)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (BtnACaption # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, 'A;' + BtnACaption)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (BtnB # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, 'B;' + BtnB)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (BtnC # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, 'C;' + BtnC)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if (BtnD # 0)</l>
<l>    fwrite_string (FileHandle, 'D;' + BtnD)//[GUILanguageToUse])</l>
<l>    fnew_line (FileHandle)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>close_file (FileHandle)</l>
<l>* set_system ('filename_encoding', 'locale')</l>
<c></c>
<c>* </c>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="ButtonsIntervaceViaFile">
<parameters>
<parameter id="Btn0FlagTeachInSuccessfull"/>
<parameter id="Btn1"/>
<parameter id="Btn2"/>
<parameter id="Btn3"/>
<parameter id="Btn4"/>
<parameter id="Btn5IconArrowLeft"/>
<parameter id="Btn6IconArrowRight"/>
<parameter id="Btn7CancelDraw"/>
<parameter id="Btn8ProgressBar"/>
<parameter id="Btn9HelpText"/>
<parameter id="BtnACaption"/>
<parameter id="BtnB"/>
<parameter id="BtnC"/>
<parameter id="BtnD"/>
<parameter id="FilenameIntervaceFile"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="TeachIn_SelectImageToLearnOn">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="ImageOrig" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="gRinnenROIs" base_type="iconic" dimension="1"/>
<par name="gEjectROIs" base_type="iconic" dimension="1"/>
</io>
<oo>
<par name="ImageOrigOut" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</oo>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="FilenameProductimage" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="CameraId" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InterfaceFromGuiFileAndPath" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ProductionLoopCounter" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Segmentation_SelectSegmentationImage_BottomLight0_TopLight1_UVLight2" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="Exit" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<l>global tuple Exitcondition</l>
<l>global tuple gProductionLoopCounter</l>
<l>global tuple vector(1) gVTPathdefinitions</l>
<l>global tuple vector(1) gVTFiledefinitions </l>
<l>global tuple vector(1) gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage</l>
<c></c>
<c>* init ouput´s</c>
<l>ImageOrigOut := ImageOrig</l>
<l>ProductionLoopCounterOut := ProductionLoopCounter</l>
<l>Exit := 0</l>
<l>gSet_HDevelopDebugFlag (SystemInformations, DebugInHalcon)</l>
<l>* DebugInHalcon := 0</l>
<c></c>
<l>gGetSubObjectVariables_SingleValue (gVTPathdefinitions, 'FormatPath_Productimages', FormatPath_Productimages)</l>
<l>gGetSubObjectVariables_SingleValue (gVTFiledefinitions, 'ProductImage Prefix for Loading from Disk', FilenameProductimagePrefix)</l>
<l>gGetSubObjectVariables_SingleValue (gVTPathdefinitions, 'TempPath', InterfaceTempPath)</l>
<c></c>
<c></c>
<l>if (Exitcondition # 1)</l>
<l>    GenRegionsForButtons (ImageOrigOut, ButtonRectangles, WindowHandle, 24, 24, 400, 4)</l>
<l>    select_obj (ButtonRectangles, RectangleCancel, 1)</l>
<l>    select_obj (ButtonRectangles, RectangleLeft, 2)</l>
<l>    select_obj (ButtonRectangles, RectangleOK, 3)</l>
<l>    select_obj (ButtonRectangles, RectangleRight, 4)</l>
<l>    dev_get_system ('engine_environment', EnvironmentIsHDevelop)</l>
<l>*     if(Segmentation_SelectSegmentationImage_BottomLight0_TopLight1_UVLight2 = 2)</l>
<l>*     ImageChannel_Selection := 2</l>
<l>*     else</l>
<l>*     ImageChannel_Selection := 0</l>
<l>*     endif</l>
<l>    ImageChannel_Selection := 1</l>
<l>    if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop')</l>
<c>        </c>
<l>        gSelectAndDisplay_MultichannelImage (ImageOrigOut, Image_SelectedChannels, ImageChannel_Selection, 1, 1)</l>
<l>        dev_display (RectangleCancel)</l>
<l>        dev_display (RectangleRight)</l>
<l>        dev_display (RectangleLeft)</l>
<l>        dev_display (RectangleOK)</l>
<l>        VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleCancel, WindowHandle, gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(0)[1], 'black')</l>
<l>        VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleOK, WindowHandle, gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(1)[1], 'black')</l>
<l>        VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_Arrow (ImageOrigOut, RectangleLeft, WindowHandle, 'left', 15)</l>
<l>        VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_Arrow (ImageOrigOut, RectangleRight, WindowHandle, 'right', 15)</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>    ButtonsIntervaceViaFile (InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath, 0, gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(0)[1], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(1)[1], 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(2)[1], 0, 0, 0, 0)</l>
<l>    RedrawGrafic := 1</l>
<l>    BtnPressed := []</l>
<l>    Firstloop := 1</l>
<l>    while (1) </l>
<l>        if (RedrawGrafic = 1)</l>
<l>            RedrawGrafic := 0</l>
<l>            if(Firstloop = 1)</l>
<l>                Firstloop := 0</l>
<l>                StopLoop := 0</l>
<l>                ImageOrigOut := ImageOrig</l>
<l>            else</l>
<l>                gProductionLoopCounter := ProductionLoopCounterOut</l>
<l>                GetPreprocessedImage (gRinnenROIs.at(CameraId), gEjectROIs.at(CameraId), ImageOrigOut, 1, FormatPath_Productimages+FilenameProductimagePrefix, CameraId, StopLoop)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<c>            </c>
<l>            if (StopLoop = 1)</l>
<l>                WriteStringToGUI (DebugInHalcon, WindowHandle, InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath, gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(3)[1], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(0)[1], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(1)[1])</l>
<l>                ProductionLoopCounterOut := ProductionLoopCounterOut -1</l>
<l>                RedrawGrafic := 1</l>
<l>                wait_seconds (0.2)</l>
<l>                continue</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<c>            </c>
<l>            gSelectAndDisplay_MultichannelImage (ImageOrigOut, Image_SelectedChannels, ImageChannel_Selection, 1, 1)</l>
<l>            dev_display (gRinnenROIs.at(0))</l>
<l>            WriteStringToGUI (DebugInHalcon, WindowHandle, InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath, [gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(4)[1] + ': ' +  (ProductionLoopCounterOut +1)], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(0)[1], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(1)[1])</l>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop')</l>
<l>                dev_display (RectangleCancel)</l>
<l>                dev_display (RectangleRight)</l>
<l>                dev_display (RectangleLeft)</l>
<l>                dev_display (RectangleOK)</l>
<l>                VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleCancel, WindowHandle, gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(0)[1], 'black')</l>
<l>                VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleOK, WindowHandle, gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(1)[1], 'black')</l>
<l>                VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_Arrow (ImageOrigOut, RectangleLeft, WindowHandle, 'left', 15)</l>
<l>                VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_Arrow (ImageOrigOut, RectangleRight, WindowHandle, 'right', 15)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>        endif </l>
<l>        Error:=[]</l>
<l>        if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop')</l>
<l>            dev_error_var (ErrorVar, 1)</l>
<l>            dev_set_check ('~give_error')</l>
<l>            get_mposition (WindowHandle, Row, Column, Button)</l>
<l>            Error := ErrorVar</l>
<l>            dev_set_check ('give_error')</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        UserIO_MonitorFile_GetBtnPress (InterfaceFromGuiFileAndPath, BtnPressed)</l>
<l>        if (BtnPressed = [])</l>
<c>            * do something so output will not freeze</c>
<l>            wait_seconds(0.05)</l>
<l>        else</l>
<l>            WriteStringToGUI (DebugInHalcon, WindowHandle, InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath, [gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(4)[1] + ': '+ (ProductionLoopCounterOut+1)], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(0)[1], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(1)[1])</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<c>        </c>
<l>        IsInside:=0</l>
<l>        if(Exitcondition = 1)</l>
<l>            break</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        if (Error = 2 or BtnPressed # [])</l>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop' and BtnPressed = [])</l>
<l>                test_region_point (RectangleCancel, Row, Column, IsInside)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            if (IsInside = 1 or BtnPressed = 1)</l>
<l>                Exitcondition := 1</l>
<l>                break</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<c>            * check if left is rectangle pressed</c>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop' and BtnPressed = [])</l>
<l>                test_region_point (RectangleLeft, Row, Column, IsInside)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            if (IsInside = 1 or BtnPressed = 5)</l>
<l>                if (ProductionLoopCounterOut &gt; 0)</l>
<l>                    ProductionLoopCounterOut := ProductionLoopCounterOut -1</l>
<l>                    RedrawGrafic := 1</l>
<l>                    continue</l>
<l>                else</l>
<l>                    WriteStringToGUI (DebugInHalcon, WindowHandle, InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath, gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(5)[1], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(0)[1], gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(1)[1])</l>
<l>                    wait_seconds(1)</l>
<l>                    RedrawGrafic := 1</l>
<l>                    continue</l>
<l>                endif</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<c>            * check if right is rectangle pressed</c>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop' and BtnPressed = [])</l>
<l>                test_region_point (RectangleRight, Row, Column, IsInside)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            if (IsInside = 1 or BtnPressed = 6)</l>
<l>                ProductionLoopCounterOut := ProductionLoopCounterOut +1</l>
<l>                RedrawGrafic := 1</l>
<l>                continue</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<c>            * check if ok is rectangle pressed</c>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop' and BtnPressed = [])</l>
<l>                test_region_point (RectangleOK, Row, Column, IsInside)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            if (IsInside = 1 or BtnPressed = 2)</l>
<l>                break</l>
<l>            endif </l>
<l>        endif </l>
<l>    endwhile</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c></c>
<l>GetSubObjectVariables_Local (gVTFiledefinitions, 'ProductImage Current Format', VTempVariable)</l>
<l>ProductImageCurrentFormat := VTempVariable.at(0)[1]</l>
<l>write_image (Image_SelectedChannels, 'tiff', 0, ProductImageCurrentFormat + '.tiff')</l>
<l>write_image (ImageOrigOut, 'tiff', 0, ProductImageCurrentFormat + 'AllChannels' + '.tiff')</l>
<c></c>
<l>if (Exitcondition = 1)</l>
<l>    Exit := true</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c></c>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="TeachIn_SelectImageToLearnOn">
<parameters>
<parameter id="CameraId"/>
<parameter id="Exit"/>
<parameter id="FilenameProductimage"/>
<parameter id="ImageOrig"/>
<parameter id="ImageOrigOut"/>
<parameter id="InterfaceFromGuiFileAndPath"/>
<parameter id="InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath"/>
<parameter id="ProductionLoopCounter"/>
<parameter id="Segmentation_SelectSegmentationImage_BottomLight0_TopLight1_UVLight2"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
<parameter id="gEjectROIs"/>
<parameter id="gRinnenROIs"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="UserIO_SetRectangleRegion">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="Image" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</io>
<oo>
<par name="Rectangle_HandlingMainRegion" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</oo>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InitPositionRow" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InitPositionColumn" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ExternalUserIOFile" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="SizeHorizontal" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="SizeHorizontalMin" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="SizeVertical" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="SizeVerticalMin" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="HandlingRectangleSize" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="MessageToDisplay" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="In_Select_ImageOut_FirstChannels0_SecondChannel1_UVChannel2" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="ExternalIO_BtnPressed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RectangleOutput_Width" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RectangleOutput_Height" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RectangleOutput_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RectangleOutput_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<c>* do some relative calulation to have the manual touching points squared and in similar size- independant from zooming</c>
<l>get_window_extents (WindowHandle, _, _, WindowHandle_Width, WindowHandle_Height)</l>
<l>get_image_size (Image, Width, Height)</l>
<l>ScaleFactor_Horizontal := Width*1.0/WindowHandle_Width</l>
<l>ScaleFactor_Vertical := Height*1.0/WindowHandle_Height</l>
<l>dev_set_draw ('margin')</l>
<l>dev_set_line_width (2)</l>
<c></c>
<c></c>
<c>* correct if init position is outside the window</c>
<l>* if (InitPositionRow &gt;= WindowHandle_Width)</l>
<l>* InitPositionRow := WindowHandle_Width/2</l>
<l>* endif</l>
<l>* if (InitPositionColumn &gt;= WindowHandle_Height)</l>
<l>* InitPositionColumn := WindowHandle_Height/2</l>
<l>* endif</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* check if the coordinates calculated are within the limits of the vizu window. possibly the initi position is out on some small images</c>
<l>if(InitPositionColumn &gt;= Width)</l>
<l>    InitPositionColumn := Width/2</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>if(InitPositionRow &gt;= Height)</l>
<l>    InitPositionRow := Height/2</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol := [InitPositionRow- SizeVertical/2,InitPositionColumn-SizeHorizontal/2]</l>
<l>PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol := [InitPositionRow+ SizeVertical/2,InitPositionColumn+SizeHorizontal/2]</l>
<c></c>
<l>gSet_HDevelopDebugFlag (SystemInformations, DebugInHalcon)</l>
<c></c>
<l>MessageToDisplay  := []</l>
<l>UserIO_SelectRectangleRegion_Visu (Image, Rectangle_HandlingMainRegion, Rectangle_HandlingLeftUpper, Rectangle_HandlingLeftLower, Rectangle_HandlingRightUpper, Rectangle_HandlingRightLower, WindowHandle, MessageToDisplay, DebugInHalcon, 0, PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol, PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol, ScaleFactor_Horizontal, ScaleFactor_Vertical, HandlingRectangleSize, In_Select_ImageOut_FirstChannels0_SecondChannel1_UVChannel2)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>if ((MessageToDisplay # '' or MessageToDisplay # []) and DebugInHalcon = 1)</l>
<l>    dev_disp_text (MessageToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'left', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>global def tuple ExternalBtnPressed</l>
<l>ExternalBtnPressed := []</l>
<l>global def tuple UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO</l>
<l>UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO := []</l>
<l>global tuple vector(1) gVTTabletInspection</l>
<l>GetSubObjectVariables_SingleValue_Local (gVTTabletInspection, 'V_SegmentationThreshold', SegmentationThreshold)</l>
<l>GetSubObjectVariables_SingleValue_Local (gVTTabletInspection, 'V_Segmentation_ColourSupport_Active', Segmentation_ColourSupport_Active)</l>
<l>GetSubObjectVariables_SingleValue_Local (gVTTabletInspection, 'V_Segmentation_ColourSupport_Threshold_Min', Segmentation_ColourSupport_Threshold_Min)</l>
<l>GetSubObjectVariables_SingleValue_Local (gVTTabletInspection, 'V_Segmentation_ColourSupport_Threshold_Max', Segmentation_ColourSupport_Threshold_Max)</l>
<c></c>
<l>LineProfileIsCurrentlyShown := 0</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* start external thread to react on gui events</c>
<l>par_start&lt;ThreadID&gt; : UserIO_MonitorFileIO (ExternalUserIOFile, 2)</l>
<c>* current rectangle for input</c>
<l>CurRectIn := 0</l>
<l>CurRectOut := 0</l>
<l>while (1)</l>
<l>    dev_error_var (ErrorVar, 1)</l>
<l>    dev_set_check ('~give_error')</l>
<l>    get_mposition (WindowHandle, Mouse_Row, Mouse_Column, MouseButton)</l>
<l>    Error := ErrorVar</l>
<l>    dev_set_check ('give_error')</l>
<l>*     wait_seconds (0.05)</l>
<c>    </c>
<l>    if (MouseButton = 1) // if it is necessary to drag region around</l>
<l>        UserIO_SelectRectangleRegion_CalculatePosition (Rectangle_HandlingMainRegion, Rectangle_HandlingLeftUpper, Rectangle_HandlingLeftLower, Rectangle_HandlingRightUpper, Rectangle_HandlingRightLower, PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol, PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol, SizeHorizontalMin, SizeVerticalMin, Mouse_Row, Mouse_Column, CurRectIn, PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol, PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol, IsInsideAHandlingRegion, CurRectOut)</l>
<l>        CurRectIn := CurRectOut</l>
<l>        if (IsInsideAHandlingRegion &gt; 0)</l>
<l>            UserIO_SelectRectangleRegion_Visu (Image, Rectangle_HandlingMainRegion, Rectangle_HandlingLeftUpper, Rectangle_HandlingLeftLower, Rectangle_HandlingRightUpper, Rectangle_HandlingRightLower, WindowHandle, MessageToDisplay, DebugInHalcon, 0, PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol, PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol, ScaleFactor_Horizontal, ScaleFactor_Vertical, HandlingRectangleSize, In_Select_ImageOut_FirstChannels0_SecondChannel1_UVChannel2)</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>    elseif (MouseButton == 0)</l>
<l>        CurRectOut := 0</l>
<l>        CurRectIn := 0</l>
<l>    else</l>
<l>        if (MouseButton = 4 or ExternalBtnPressed # [])</l>
<l>            if (ExternalBtnPressed = 3) // 3 is button for line profile</l>
<l>                ExternalBtnPressed := []</l>
<l>                if (LineProfileIsCurrentlyShown = 0)</l>
<l>                    set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'false')</l>
<l>                    get_part (WindowHandle, WindowVizuPartBackupR1C1R2C2.at(0), WindowVizuPartBackupR1C1R2C2.at(1), WindowVizuPartBackupR1C1R2C2.at(2), WindowVizuPartBackupR1C1R2C2.at(3))</l>
<l>                    dev_set_part (PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol[0], PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol[1], PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol[0], PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol[1])</l>
<l>                    set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'false') </l>
<l>                    TeachIn_ShowLineProfile (Image, PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol, PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol, WindowHandle, SegmentationThreshold, Segmentation_ColourSupport_Active, Segmentation_ColourSupport_Threshold_Min, Segmentation_ColourSupport_Threshold_Max, In_Select_ImageOut_FirstChannels0_SecondChannel1_UVChannel2)</l>
<l>                    flush_buffer (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>                    set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'true')</l>
<l>                    LineProfileIsCurrentlyShown := 1</l>
<l>                else</l>
<l>                    dev_set_part (WindowVizuPartBackupR1C1R2C2.at(0), WindowVizuPartBackupR1C1R2C2.at(1), WindowVizuPartBackupR1C1R2C2.at(2), WindowVizuPartBackupR1C1R2C2.at(3))</l>
<l>                    LineProfileIsCurrentlyShown := 0</l>
<l>                    UserIO_SelectRectangleRegion_Visu (Image, Rectangle_HandlingMainRegion, Rectangle_HandlingLeftUpper, Rectangle_HandlingLeftLower, Rectangle_HandlingRightUpper, Rectangle_HandlingRightLower, WindowHandle, MessageToDisplay, DebugInHalcon, 0, PositionRectangle_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol, PositionRectangle_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol, ScaleFactor_Horizontal, ScaleFactor_Vertical, HandlingRectangleSize, In_Select_ImageOut_FirstChannels0_SecondChannel1_UVChannel2)</l>
<l>                endif</l>
<l>                continue</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            break</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>endwhile</l>
<c>* clean up external thread</c>
<l>UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO := 1</l>
<l>par_join (ThreadID)</l>
<l>UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO := 0</l>
<c></c>
<l>ExternalIO_BtnPressed := ExternalBtnPressed</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>smallest_rectangle1 (Rectangle_HandlingMainRegion, Row1, Column1, Row2, Column2)</l>
<l>RectangleOutput_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol := [Row1,Column1]</l>
<l>RectangleOutput_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol := [Row2,Column2]</l>
<l>RectangleOutput_Width := Column2-Column1</l>
<l>RectangleOutput_Height:= Row2-Row1</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>wait_seconds (0.1)</l>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="UserIO_SetRectangleRegion">
<parameters>
<parameter id="ExternalIO_BtnPressed"/>
<parameter id="ExternalUserIOFile"/>
<parameter id="HandlingRectangleSize"/>
<parameter id="Image"/>
<parameter id="In_Select_ImageOut_FirstChannels0_SecondChannel1_UVChannel2"/>
<parameter id="InitPositionColumn"/>
<parameter id="InitPositionRow"/>
<parameter id="MessageToDisplay"/>
<parameter id="RectangleOutput_Height"/>
<parameter id="RectangleOutput_LeftUpper_Tpl_RowCol"/>
<parameter id="RectangleOutput_RightLower_Tpl_RowCol"/>
<parameter id="RectangleOutput_Width"/>
<parameter id="Rectangle_HandlingMainRegion"/>
<parameter id="SizeHorizontal"/>
<parameter id="SizeHorizontalMin"/>
<parameter id="SizeVertical"/>
<parameter id="SizeVerticalMin"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="UserIO_MonitorFileIO">
<interface>
<ic>
<par name="ExternalUserIOFile" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="BtnBreak" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
</interface>
<body>
<l>global tuple ExternalBtnPressed</l>
<l>global tuple UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO</l>
<l>while (1)</l>
<l>    wait_seconds (0.2) </l>
<l>    file_exists (ExternalUserIOFile, FileExists)</l>
<l>    if (FileExists # 0)</l>
<l>        Error := 2</l>
<l>        open_file (ExternalUserIOFile, 'input', FileHandle)</l>
<l>        fread_line (FileHandle, OutLine, IsEOF)</l>
<l>        close_file (FileHandle)</l>
<l>        dev_set_check ('~give_error')</l>
<l>        delete_file (ExternalUserIOFile)</l>
<l>        dev_set_check ('give_error')</l>
<l>        tuple_strrchr (OutLine, '\n', Position)</l>
<l>        tuple_str_first_n (OutLine, Position-1, ExternalBtnPressed)</l>
<l>        tuple_number (ExternalBtnPressed, ExternalBtnPressed)</l>
<l>        if (ExternalBtnPressed = BtnBreak)</l>
<l>            break</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>    if (UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO = 1)</l>
<l>        break</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>endwhile</l>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="UserIO_MonitorFileIO">
<parameters>
<parameter id="BtnBreak"/>
<parameter id="ExternalUserIOFile"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="UserIO_SetPaintRegion">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="Image" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</io>
<oo>
<par name="RegionOutput" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</oo>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InitPositionRow" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InitPositionColumn" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ExternalUserIOFile" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="MessageToDisplay" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="BrushSizeFactorToWindowSize" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="VizualisationImage_FirstChannel0_SecondChannel1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="ExternalIO_BtnPressed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<l>gen_empty_obj (RegionOutput)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>get_image_size (Image, Width, Height)</l>
<c>* define relative brush size</c>
<l>get_part (WindowHandle, Row11, Column11, Row21, Column21)</l>
<l>WindowWidth := Row21-Row11</l>
<l>WindowHeight := Column21-Column11</l>
<l>RelativeBrushWidth := WindowWidth / BrushSizeFactorToWindowSize</l>
<l>RelativeBrushHeight := WindowHeight / BrushSizeFactorToWindowSize</l>
<l>if (RelativeBrushWidth &gt; RelativeBrushHeight)</l>
<l>    BrushSize := RelativeBrushWidth</l>
<l>else</l>
<l>    BrushSize := RelativeBrushHeight</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c>* prepare some visu pattern</c>
<l>gen_checker_region (RegionChecker, Width, Height, WindowWidth/50, WindowHeight/50)</l>
<l>dev_set_color (['dim gray', 'red'])</l>
<l>dev_set_draw ('margin')</l>
<l>gSelectAndDisplay_MultichannelImage (Image, Image_SelectedChannels, VizualisationImage_FirstChannel0_SecondChannel1, 1, 1)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>gSet_HDevelopDebugFlag (SystemInformations, DebugInHalcon)</l>
<c></c>
<l>if ((MessageToDisplay # '' or MessageToDisplay # []) and DebugInHalcon = 1)</l>
<l>    dev_disp_text (MessageToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'left', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>global def tuple ExternalBtnPressed</l>
<l>ExternalBtnPressed := []</l>
<l>global def tuple UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO</l>
<l>UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO := []</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* indicate the brush size to operator</c>
<l>dev_set_color ('blue')</l>
<l>get_part (WindowHandle, VisuLeftUpper_Row, VisuLeftUpper_Column, VisuRightLower_Row, VisuRightLower_Column)</l>
<l>gen_circle (Brush_SampleVisuForOperator, VisuLeftUpper_Row + 15, VisuRightLower_Column -15, BrushSize/2)</l>
<l>dev_display (Brush_SampleVisuForOperator)</l>
<l>gen_empty_obj (RegionVizu)</l>
<c></c>
<l>while (1)</l>
<l>    dev_error_var (ErrorVar, 1)</l>
<l>    dev_set_check ('~give_error')</l>
<l>    get_mposition (WindowHandle, MouseRow, MouseColumn, MouseButton)</l>
<l>    Error := ErrorVar</l>
<l>    dev_set_check ('give_error')</l>
<l>    if (MouseButton = 1)</l>
<l>        gen_circle (Brush, MouseRow, MouseColumn, BrushSize/2)</l>
<l>        union2 (RegionOutput, Brush, RegionOutput)</l>
<c>        * </c>
<l>        intersection (RegionChecker, RegionOutput, RegionVizu)</l>
<l>        concat_obj (RegionVizu, RegionOutput, RegionVizu)</l>
<c>        * </c>
<l>        set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'false')</l>
<l>        gSelectAndDisplay_MultichannelImage (Image, Image_SelectedChannels1, VizualisationImage_FirstChannel0_SecondChannel1, 1, 1)</l>
<l>        select_obj (RegionVizu, Checker, 1)</l>
<l>        dev_set_color ('dim gray')</l>
<l>        dev_display (Checker)</l>
<l>        dev_set_color ('red')</l>
<l>        select_obj (RegionVizu, Surrounding, 2)</l>
<l>        dev_display (Surrounding)</l>
<l>        dev_set_color ('blue')</l>
<l>        dev_display (Brush_SampleVisuForOperator)</l>
<c>        * </c>
<l>        if ((MessageToDisplay # '' or MessageToDisplay # []) and DebugInHalcon = 1)</l>
<l>            dev_disp_text (MessageToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'left', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        flush_buffer (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>        set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'true')</l>
<l>    else</l>
<l>        par_start&lt;ThreadID&gt; : UserIO_MonitorFileIO (ExternalUserIOFile, 2)</l>
<l>        UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO := 1</l>
<l>        par_join (ThreadID)</l>
<l>        if (MouseButton = 4)</l>
<l>            break</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        if (ExternalBtnPressed = 5 or ExternalBtnPressed = 6)</l>
<l>            if (ExternalBtnPressed = 5) // brush smaller request</l>
<l>                BrushSize := BrushSize * 0.7</l>
<l>                if (BrushSize &lt; 3)</l>
<l>                    BrushSize := 3</l>
<l>                endif</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            if (ExternalBtnPressed = 6) // brush bigger request</l>
<l>                BrushSize := BrushSize * 1.3</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<c></c>
<c>            * indicate the brush size to operator</c>
<l>            dev_set_color ('blue')</l>
<l>            gen_circle (Brush_SampleVisuForOperator, BrushSize/2 + VisuLeftUpper_Row + 15, VisuRightLower_Column - BrushSize/2 -15, BrushSize/2)</l>
<c>            </c>
<l>            set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'false')</l>
<l>            gSelectAndDisplay_MultichannelImage (Image, Image_SelectedChannels2, VizualisationImage_FirstChannel0_SecondChannel1, 1, 1)</l>
<l>            select_obj (RegionVizu, Checker, 1)</l>
<l>            dev_set_color ('dim gray')</l>
<l>            dev_display (Checker)</l>
<l>            dev_set_color ('red')</l>
<l>            select_obj (RegionVizu, Surrounding, 2)</l>
<l>            dev_display (Surrounding)</l>
<l>            dev_set_color ('blue')</l>
<l>            dev_display (Brush_SampleVisuForOperator)</l>
<c>            * </c>
<l>            if ((MessageToDisplay # '' or MessageToDisplay # []) and DebugInHalcon = 1)</l>
<l>                dev_disp_text (MessageToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'left', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            flush_buffer (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>            set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'true')</l>
<l>            ExternalBtnPressed := []</l>
<l>            continue</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        if ( ExternalBtnPressed # []) // handles other external button interactions</l>
<l>            break</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>    endif  </l>
<l>endwhile</l>
<l>ExternalIO_BtnPressed := ExternalBtnPressed</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<l>dev_set_color ('red')</l>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="UserIO_SetPaintRegion">
<parameters>
<parameter id="BrushSizeFactorToWindowSize"/>
<parameter id="ExternalIO_BtnPressed"/>
<parameter id="ExternalUserIOFile"/>
<parameter id="Image"/>
<parameter id="InitPositionColumn"/>
<parameter id="InitPositionRow"/>
<parameter id="MessageToDisplay"/>
<parameter id="RegionOutput"/>
<parameter id="VizualisationImage_FirstChannel0_SecondChannel1"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="CalculateColourClassification">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="ImageOrig" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Colour_InnerRegion" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Colour_OuterRegion" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Colour_Background" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</io>
<oo>
<par name="ImageClass" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Classified_Tablets" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</oo>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="SecondClassificationStepForLearning" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ColourLearning_Tolerance" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ColourLearning_MaxIterations" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ColourLearning_NumHidden" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ColourLearning_MedianTrainImage_FilterSize" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InnerColour_Median" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ColourClassificationFilename" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="MessageToDisplayDuringTraining" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="ColourClassificationHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<l>NumberOfClasses := 3</l>
<c></c>
<l>copy_obj (Colour_InnerRegion, Classes, 1, 1)</l>
<l>ColourMean (ImageOrig, Colour_InnerRegion, Mean_Red1, Mean_Green1, Mean_Blue1)</l>
<l>if (InnerColour_Median = 1)</l>
<c>    * filter the selected area to get more stable results for learning</c>
<l>    reduce_domain (ImageOrig, Classes, ImageReduced)</l>
<l>    median_image (ImageReduced, ImageMedian, 'circle', 2, 'mirrored')</l>
<l>    overpaint_gray (ImageOrig, ImageMedian)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c></c>
<l>concat_obj (Colour_InnerRegion, Colour_OuterRegion, Classes)</l>
<l>ColourMean (ImageOrig, Colour_OuterRegion, Mean_Red2, Mean_Green2, Mean_Blue2)</l>
<c></c>
<c>* filter the selected area to get more stabel results for learning</c>
<l>reduce_domain (ImageOrig, Colour_OuterRegion, ImageReduced)</l>
<l>median_image (ImageReduced, ImageMedian, 'circle', 3, 'mirrored')</l>
<c>* leave overpaint for background as optional. on fine print on capsule it can be problematic to manipulate color</c>
<l>if(0)</l>
<l>    overpaint_gray (ImageOrig, ImageMedian)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c></c>
<l>concat_obj (Classes, Colour_Background, Classes)</l>
<c>* filter the selected area to get more stabel results for learning</c>
<l>reduce_domain (ImageOrig, Colour_Background, ImageReduced)</l>
<l>median_image (ImageReduced, ImageMedian, 'circle', 3, 'mirrored')</l>
<l>overpaint_gray (ImageOrig, ImageMedian)</l>
<c></c>
<l>get_image_pointer1 (ImageOrig, _, _, Width, Height)</l>
<l>dev_set_part (0, 0, Height, Width)</l>
<l>dev_display (ImageOrig)</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<l>GUILanguageToUse := 0 //standard language is english</l>
<l>gSet_HDevelopDebugFlag (SystemInformations, DebugInHalcon)</l>
<c></c>
<l>if (DebugInHalcon = 1)</l>
<l>    dev_disp_text (MessageToDisplayDuringTraining, 'window', 'top', 'left', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c></c>
<c>* Create the classifier and add the samples</c>
<l>set_system ('parallelize_operators', 'true')</l>
<c></c>
<c>********************* the classification preperation</c>
<c>* Create the classifier and add the samples</c>
<l>create_class_mlp (3, ColourLearning_NumHidden, 3, 'softmax', 'normalization', 3, 42, MLPHandle)</l>
<l>set_rejection_params_class_mlp (MLPHandle, 'sampling_strategy', 'hyperbox_around_all_classes')</l>
<l>set_rejection_params_class_mlp (MLPHandle, 'hyperbox_tolerance', ColourLearning_Tolerance)</l>
<c>* filter the image a bit</c>
<l>if (ColourLearning_MedianTrainImage_FilterSize &gt;=1)</l>
<l>    median_image (ImageOrig, ImageForTraining, 'circle', ColourLearning_MedianTrainImage_FilterSize, 'mirrored')</l>
<l>else</l>
<l>    copy_obj (ImageOrig, ImageForTraining, 1, -1)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>add_samples_image_class_mlp (ImageForTraining, Classes, MLPHandle)</l>
<c>* Train the classifier</c>
<l>train_class_mlp (MLPHandle, ColourLearning_MaxIterations, 1, 0.01, Error, ErrorLog)</l>
<c>*********************</c>
<c></c>
<l>create_class_lut_mlp (MLPHandle, [], [], ColourClassificationHandle)</l>
<l>classify_image_class_lut (ImageOrig, ClassRegions, ColourClassificationHandle)</l>
<c></c>
<l>region_to_mean (ClassRegions, ImageOrig, ImageClass)</l>
<l>dev_display (ImageClass)</l>
<l>select_obj (ClassRegions, TabletClassified, 1)</l>
<l>dev_set_color ('magenta')</l>
<l>dev_display (TabletClassified)</l>
<c></c>
<l>select_obj (ClassRegions, Classified_PrintOrMirror, 2)</l>
<l>dev_set_color ('cyan')</l>
<l>dev_display (Classified_PrintOrMirror)</l>
<c></c>
<c></c>
<l>connection (TabletClassified, ConnectedRegions)</l>
<l>select_shape (ConnectedRegions, Tablets, 'area', 'and', 6000, 9999999)</l>
<l>union1 (Tablets, Tablets)</l>
<l>if (SecondClassificationStepForLearning = 1)</l>
<c>    * build up new classificator</c>
<l>    clear_class_lut (ColourClassificationHandle)</l>
<l>    gen_empty_obj (NewClasses)</l>
<l>    count_obj (Classes, NumberOfClasses)</l>
<l>    concat_obj (NewClasses, Tablets, NewClasses)</l>
<l>    if (NumberOfClasses&gt;1)</l>
<l>        for Index := 2 to NumberOfClasses by 1</l>
<l>            select_obj (Classes, ObjectSelected, Index)</l>
<l>            concat_obj (NewClasses, ObjectSelected, NewClasses)</l>
<l>        endfor</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>    create_class_mlp (3, 10, 3, 'softmax', 'principal_components', 3, 42, MLPHandle)</l>
<l>    set_rejection_params_class_mlp (MLPHandle, 'sampling_strategy', 'hyperbox_around_all_classes')</l>
<l>    set_rejection_params_class_mlp (MLPHandle, 'hyperbox_tolerance', ColourLearning_Tolerance)</l>
<l>    add_samples_image_class_mlp (ImageOrig, NewClasses, MLPHandle)</l>
<l>    train_class_mlp (MLPHandle, 200, 1, 0.01, Error, ErrorLog)</l>
<l>    create_class_lut_mlp (MLPHandle, [], [], ColourClassificationHandle)</l>
<l>    classify_image_class_lut (ImageMedian, ClassRegions, ColourClassificationHandle)</l>
<l>    region_to_mean (ClassRegions, ImageOrig, ImageClass)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>dev_display (ImageClass)</l>
<l>dev_set_draw ('margin')</l>
<l>dev_set_color ('yellow')</l>
<l>select_obj (ClassRegions, Classified_Tablets, 1)</l>
<l>dev_display (Classified_Tablets)</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>set_system ('parallelize_operators', 'false')</l>
<c></c>
<l>write_class_mlp (MLPHandle, ColourClassificationFilename)</l>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="CalculateColourClassification">
<parameters>
<parameter id="Classified_Tablets"/>
<parameter id="ColourClassificationFilename"/>
<parameter id="ColourClassificationHandle"/>
<parameter id="ColourLearning_MaxIterations"/>
<parameter id="ColourLearning_MedianTrainImage_FilterSize"/>
<parameter id="ColourLearning_NumHidden"/>
<parameter id="ColourLearning_Tolerance"/>
<parameter id="Colour_Background"/>
<parameter id="Colour_InnerRegion"/>
<parameter id="Colour_OuterRegion"/>
<parameter id="ImageClass"/>
<parameter id="ImageOrig"/>
<parameter id="InnerColour_Median"/>
<parameter id="MessageToDisplayDuringTraining"/>
<parameter id="SecondClassificationStepForLearning"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="UserIO_MonitorFile_GetBtnPress">
<interface>
<ic>
<par name="BtnFilenameWithPath" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="BtnPressed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<l>file_exists (BtnFilenameWithPath, FileExists)</l>
<l>if (FileExists # 0)</l>
<l>    Error := 2</l>
<l>    open_file (BtnFilenameWithPath, 'input', FileHandle)</l>
<l>    fread_line (FileHandle, OutLine, IsEOF)</l>
<l>    close_file (FileHandle)</l>
<l>    dev_set_check ('~give_error')</l>
<l>    delete_file (BtnFilenameWithPath)</l>
<l>    dev_set_check ('give_error')</l>
<l>    tuple_strrchr (OutLine, '\n', Position)</l>
<l>    tuple_str_first_n (OutLine, Position-1, BtnPressed)</l>
<l>    tuple_number (BtnPressed, BtnPressed)</l>
<l>else</l>
<l>    BtnPressed := []</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="UserIO_MonitorFile_GetBtnPress">
<parameters>
<parameter id="BtnFilenameWithPath"/>
<parameter id="BtnPressed"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="UserIO_SetHorizontalLines">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="Image" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</io>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InitPositionLine1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InitPositionLine2" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ExternalUserIOFile" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="MessageToDisplay" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="LeftBorderUsed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RightBorderUsed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RangeOfXValues" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Colour" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ShowCurrentValues" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ToleranceInversionAllowed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ToleranceProposal_ScaleIsMaxValue" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="PositionLine1" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="PositionLine2" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ExternalIO_BtnPressed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<l>global tuple vector(1) gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage</l>
<l>BorderWasMoved_Left := 0</l>
<l>BorderWasMoved_Right := 0</l>
<l>ToleranceInverted := 0</l>
<c></c>
<c>*disable right mouse menue in hdevelop</c>
<l>dev_set_preferences ('graphics_window_context_menu', 'false')</l>
<c></c>
<l>tuple_mean (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl, Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Mean)</l>
<l>tuple_deviation (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl, Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Deviation)</l>
<c></c>
<c></c>
<l>get_image_size (Image, Width, Height)</l>
<l>dev_set_part (0, 0, Height-1, Width-1)</l>
<l>dev_clear_window ()</l>
<l>dev_display (Image)</l>
<l>if(Colour # -1 or Colour # [])</l>
<l>    dev_set_color (Colour)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>PositionLine1 := InitPositionLine1</l>
<l>PositionLine2 := InitPositionLine2</l>
<c></c>
<l>gSet_HDevelopDebugFlag (SystemInformations, DebugInHalcon)</l>
<l>* DebugInHalcon := 0</l>
<c></c>
<l>if ((MessageToDisplay # '' or MessageToDisplay # []) and DebugInHalcon = 1)</l>
<l>    dev_disp_text (MessageToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'center', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine1, Height, PositionLine1)</l>
<l>disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine2, Height, PositionLine2)</l>
<c></c>
<l>get_window_extents (WindowHandle, _, _, WindowWidth, WindowHeight)</l>
<l>DivisionPerSegment := (RightBorderUsed - LeftBorderUsed)*1.0 / RangeOfXValues</l>
<c></c>
<c>* do some calculation for 6Sigma tolerance approach start here</c>
<l>Sigma := 3</l>
<l>* Sigma := 6</l>
<c></c>
<l>dev_set_color ('#ffff0055')</l>
<l>PositionLineMean := PositionLine1 + Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Mean * DivisionPerSegment</l>
<c></c>
<l>UserIO_CheckIfSigmaBoundariesAreInRange (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Mean - (Sigma*Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Deviation), RangeOfXValues, ToleranceProposal_ScaleIsMaxValue, ThreeSigmaLeft)</l>
<l>UserIO_CheckIfSigmaBoundariesAreInRange (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Mean + (Sigma*Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Deviation), RangeOfXValues, ToleranceProposal_ScaleIsMaxValue, ThreeSigmaRight)</l>
<l>PositionLine_SigmaLeft := PositionLine1 + (ThreeSigmaLeft * DivisionPerSegment)</l>
<l>PositionLine_SigmaRight := PositionLine1 + (ThreeSigmaRight * DivisionPerSegment)</l>
<c></c>
<l>disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLineMean, Height, PositionLineMean)</l>
<l>disp_line (WindowHandle, Height/2, PositionLine_SigmaLeft, Height, PositionLine_SigmaLeft)</l>
<l>disp_line (WindowHandle, Height/2, PositionLine_SigmaRight, Height, PositionLine_SigmaRight)</l>
<c></c>
<l>tuple_min (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl, Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Min)</l>
<l>tuple_max (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl, Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Max)</l>
<l>PositionLine_Min := PositionLine1 + (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Min * DivisionPerSegment)</l>
<l>PositionLine_Max := PositionLine1 + (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Max * DivisionPerSegment)</l>
<c></c>
<l>dev_set_color ('#ffff0099')</l>
<l>disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine_Min, Height/2, PositionLine_Min)</l>
<l>disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine_Max, Height/2, PositionLine_Max)</l>
<c></c>
<l>TextToDisplay :=[]</l>
<l>TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(39)[1] + ' = '+(Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Mean)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(43)[1]  + ' = ' + (ThreeSigmaLeft)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(44)[1] + ' = ' + (ThreeSigmaRight)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(40)[1] +  ' = ' + (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Min)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(41)[1]  + ' = ' + (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Max)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,('Count'  + ' = ' + |Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl|) ]</l>
<c></c>
<l>dev_disp_text (TextToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'right', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<c>* do some calculation for 6Sigma tolerance approach end here</c>
<c>* </c>
<l>global def tuple ExternalBtnPressed</l>
<l>ExternalBtnPressed := []</l>
<l>global def tuple UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO</l>
<l>UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO := []</l>
<c>* </c>
<l>par_start&lt;ThreadID&gt; : UserIO_MonitorFileIO (ExternalUserIOFile, 2)</l>
<l>MouseButton := []</l>
<l>ForceVisuUpdate := 0</l>
<l>wait_seconds(0.3)</l>
<l>while (1)</l>
<l>    dev_error_var (ErrorVar, 1)</l>
<l>    dev_set_check ('~give_error')</l>
<l>    get_mposition (WindowHandle, Row, Column, MouseButton)</l>
<l>    Error := ErrorVar</l>
<l>    dev_set_check ('give_error')</l>
<l>    if (MouseButton = 1 or ForceVisuUpdate = 1)</l>
<l>        set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'false')</l>
<l>        dev_display (Image)</l>
<c>        </c>
<l>        if (ForceVisuUpdate = 0)</l>
<l>            distance_pl (Row, Column, 0, PositionLine1, Height, PositionLine1, DistanceToLine1)</l>
<l>            distance_pl (Row, Column, 0, PositionLine2, Height, PositionLine2, DistanceToLine2)</l>
<l>            if (DistanceToLine1 &lt;= DistanceToLine2)</l>
<l>                PositionLine1 := Column</l>
<l>                BorderWasMoved_Left := 1</l>
<l>                if (PositionLine2 - PositionLine1 &lt; DivisionPerSegment) // make shure there is a mindistance of one value</l>
<l>                    PositionLine1 := PositionLine2 - DivisionPerSegment - 0.001</l>
<l>                endif</l>
<l>            else</l>
<l>                PositionLine2 := Column</l>
<l>                BorderWasMoved_Right := 1</l>
<l>                if (PositionLine2 - PositionLine1 &lt; DivisionPerSegment) // make shure there is a mindistance of one value</l>
<l>                    PositionLine2 := PositionLine1 + DivisionPerSegment + 0.001</l>
<l>                endif</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders := (PositionLine1 - LeftBorderUsed) / DivisionPerSegment</l>
<l>            if (PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders &lt;=0)</l>
<l>                PositionLine1 := LeftBorderUsed   </l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders := (PositionLine2 - LeftBorderUsed) / DivisionPerSegment        </l>
<l>            if (PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders &gt;=RangeOfXValues)</l>
<l>                PositionLine2 := RightBorderUsed</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        ForceVisuUpdate := 0</l>
<l>        dev_set_color ('yellow')</l>
<l>        disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine1, Height, PositionLine1)</l>
<l>        PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders := (PositionLine1 - LeftBorderUsed) / DivisionPerSegment</l>
<l>        disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine2, Height, PositionLine2)</l>
<l>        PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders := (PositionLine2 - LeftBorderUsed) / DivisionPerSegment</l>
<l>        if(ShowCurrentValues = 1)</l>
<l>            tuple_round (PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders, PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders)</l>
<l>            dev_disp_text (PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders, 'image', WindowHeight/2 + 40, PositionLine1 -45, 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>            tuple_round (PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders, PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders)</l>
<l>            dev_disp_text (PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders, 'image', WindowHeight/2 - 60, PositionLine2, 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>            TextToDisplay := []</l>
<c>            * display sigma and mean data</c>
<l>            TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(39)[1] + ' = '+(Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Mean)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>            TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(43)[1]  + ' = ' + (ThreeSigmaLeft)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>            TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(44)[1] + ' = ' + (ThreeSigmaRight)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>            TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(40)[1] +  ' = ' + (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Min)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>            TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(41)[1]  + ' = ' + (Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl_Max)$'6.1f')]</l>
<l>            if (ToleranceInverted = 0)</l>
<l>                TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(42)[1] + ' =  ' + (PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders - PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders))]</l>
<l>            else</l>
<l>                TextToDisplay := [TextToDisplay,(gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(42)[1] + ' =  ' + (255 - (PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders - PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders)))]</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            dev_disp_text (TextToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'right', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        if ((MessageToDisplay # '' or MessageToDisplay # []) and DebugInHalcon = 1)</l>
<l>            dev_disp_text (MessageToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'center', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<c>        * display transparent tolernace region</c>
<l>        dev_set_color ('#ffff0055')</l>
<l>        if(ToleranceInverted = 0)</l>
<l>            gen_rectangle1 (ToleranceVisualization, WindowHeight/2 - 30, PositionLine1, WindowHeight/2 + 30, PositionLine2)</l>
<l>        else</l>
<l>            gen_rectangle1 (ToleranceVisualization1, WindowHeight/2 - 30, InitPositionLine1, WindowHeight/2 + 30, PositionLine1)</l>
<l>            gen_rectangle1 (ToleranceVisualization2, WindowHeight/2 - 30, PositionLine2, WindowHeight/2 + 30, InitPositionLine2)</l>
<l>            concat_obj (ToleranceVisualization1, ToleranceVisualization2, ToleranceVisualization)  </l>
<l>            union1 (ToleranceVisualization, ToleranceVisualization)</l>
<l>        endif </l>
<l>        dev_set_draw ('fill')</l>
<l>        dev_display (ToleranceVisualization)</l>
<l>        dev_set_draw ('margin')</l>
<c>        </c>
<l>        dev_set_color ('#ffff0040')</l>
<l>        disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLineMean, Height, PositionLineMean)</l>
<l>        disp_line (WindowHandle, Height/2, PositionLine_SigmaLeft, Height, PositionLine_SigmaLeft)</l>
<l>        disp_line (WindowHandle, Height/2, PositionLine_SigmaRight, Height, PositionLine_SigmaRight)</l>
<l>        dev_set_color ('#ffff0099')</l>
<l>        disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine_Min, Height/2, PositionLine_Min)</l>
<l>        disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine_Max, Height/2, PositionLine_Max)</l>
<c></c>
<l>        flush_buffer (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>        set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'true')</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>    if (MouseButton = 4 or ExternalBtnPressed # [])</l>
<l>        if (ExternalBtnPressed = 3)</l>
<l>            if (ToleranceInverted = 0)</l>
<l>                ToleranceInverted := 1</l>
<l>            else</l>
<l>                ToleranceInverted := 0</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            ExternalBtnPressed := []</l>
<l>            ForceVisuUpdate := 1</l>
<l>            continue</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        if ( BorderWasMoved_Left = 1 and BorderWasMoved_Right = 1 or ExternalBtnPressed = 2 or ExternalBtnPressed = 1)</l>
<l>            UserIO_Stop_MonitoringFileIO := 1</l>
<l>            par_join (ThreadID)</l>
<l>            break</l>
<l>        else</l>
<l>            OperatorHint := gVTMessagesInLocalLanguage.at(45)[1] // hint to set tolerances first</l>
<l>            dev_disp_text (OperatorHint, 'window', 'center', 'center', 'red', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>            ExternalBtnPressed:=[]</l>
<l>            wait_seconds(2)</l>
<l>            dev_clear_window ()</l>
<l>            dev_display (Image)</l>
<l>            if (MessageToDisplay # '' or MessageToDisplay # [])</l>
<l>                dev_disp_text (MessageToDisplay, 'window', 'top', 'center', 'blue', ['box_color','box_padding'], ['#ffffff77',5])</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine1, Height, PositionLine1)</l>
<l>            disp_line (WindowHandle, 0, PositionLine2, Height, PositionLine2)</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>endwhile</l>
<c></c>
<l>if (ToleranceInverted = 1) // indicate via twisted tolerances that the inversion took place</l>
<l>    TempValue := PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders</l>
<l>    PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders := PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders</l>
<l>    PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders := TempValue</l>
<l>*     stop()</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c></c>
<l>ExternalIO_BtnPressed := ExternalBtnPressed</l>
<c></c>
<c>*disable right mouse menue in hdevelop</c>
<l>dev_set_preferences ('graphics_window_context_menu', 'true')</l>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="UserIO_SetHorizontalLines">
<parameters>
<parameter id="Calculation_Colour_Mean_tpl"/>
<parameter id="Colour"/>
<parameter id="ExternalIO_BtnPressed"/>
<parameter id="ExternalUserIOFile"/>
<parameter id="Image"/>
<parameter id="InitPositionLine1"/>
<parameter id="InitPositionLine2"/>
<parameter id="LeftBorderUsed"/>
<parameter id="MessageToDisplay"/>
<parameter id="PositionLine1"/>
<parameter id="PositionLine1_RelativeToBorders"/>
<parameter id="PositionLine2"/>
<parameter id="PositionLine2_RelativeToBorders"/>
<parameter id="RangeOfXValues"/>
<parameter id="RightBorderUsed"/>
<parameter id="ShowCurrentValues"/>
<parameter id="ToleranceInversionAllowed"/>
<parameter id="ToleranceProposal_ScaleIsMaxValue"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="Plot_TupleResultsHistogramm">
<interface>
<oo>
<par name="DumpWindowWithOverlays" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</oo>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="TupleToVisualize" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Colour" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="XLabel" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="YLabel" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Ticks_X" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Visu_Max_X" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="SmoothHistogramEnable" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="LeftBorderUsed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="RightBorderUsed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<c>* max_x anpassen über vorgegebene variable? - wenn -1 dann maxwert + 10%</c>
<l>get_part (WindowHandle, Row1, Column1, Row2, Column2)</l>
<l>WindowHeight := Row2-Row1+1</l>
<l>WindowWidth := Column2-Column1+1</l>
<c></c>
<l>SortTupleToHisto (TupleToVisualize, Visu_Max_X, Max_Y, Histo, Max_X)</l>
<l>PlotParamName := ['ticks_x','margin_top','margin_left','start_y','end_y', 'end_x']</l>
<l>PlotParamValue := [Ticks_X,20,80,0,Max_Y, Max_X]</l>
<c></c>
<l>if (SmoothHistogramEnable = 1)</l>
<l>    create_funct_1d_array (Histo, Function)</l>
<l>    smooth_funct_1d_mean (Function, 19, 5, Function_Smoothed)</l>
<l>*     smooth_funct_1d_gauss (Function, 5, Function_Smoothed)</l>
<l>    funct_1d_to_pairs (Function_Smoothed, XValues, Histo)</l>
<l>    tuple_max (Histo, Max)</l>
<l>    PlotParamValue[4]:=Max</l>
<l>*     plot_funct_1d (WindowHandle, Function_Smoothed, XLabel, YLabel, Colour, PlotParamName, PlotParamValue)</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c></c>
<l>dev_clear_window ()</l>
<c></c>
<l>plot_tuple_edit (WindowHandle, [1:Max_X], Histo, XLabel, YLabel, Colour, PlotParamName, PlotParamValue, LeftBorderUsed, RightBorderUsed)</l>
<l>dump_window_image (DumpWindowWithOverlays, WindowHandle)</l>
<l>get_image_size (DumpWindowWithOverlays, DumpWindow_Width, DumpWindow_Height)</l>
<l>dev_set_part (0, 0, DumpWindow_Height, DumpWindow_Width)</l>
<l>HorizontalScale := 1.0000* WindowWidth/DumpWindow_Width</l>
<l>* dev_display (DumpWindowWithOverlays)</l>
<c></c>
<l>tuple_round (RightBorderUsed, RightBorderUsed)</l>
<l>tuple_round (LeftBorderUsed, LeftBorderUsed)</l>
<c></c>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="Plot_TupleResultsHistogramm">
<parameters>
<parameter id="Colour"/>
<parameter id="DumpWindowWithOverlays"/>
<parameter id="LeftBorderUsed"/>
<parameter id="RightBorderUsed"/>
<parameter id="SmoothHistogramEnable"/>
<parameter id="Ticks_X"/>
<parameter id="TupleToVisualize"/>
<parameter id="Visu_Max_X"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
<parameter id="XLabel"/>
<parameter id="YLabel"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="Shiftregister_RebuildCalc">
<interface>
<ic>
<par name="ControlShiftregister_TriggerRebuild" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ControlShiftregister_TriggerKill" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="ProcessingLoopcounter" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorIn" base_type="ctrl" dimension="1"/>
<par name="StepWidth_NumberOfFramesToRebuild" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorOut" base_type="ctrl" dimension="1"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<c>* Preperations for BuildingShiftregister</c>
<c>* In the vector data is - first element:</c>
<c>* first tuple element is startcount of rebuildingstep</c>
<c>* -1 is just initialized</c>
<c>* 0 is normal operation - do nothing in shiftregister</c>
<c>* 1 is rebuild shiftregister</c>
<c>* &gt;1 new request for building shiftregister</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* second tuple element is kill shiftregister when 1, else 0</c>
<c>* In the vector data is - second element:</c>
<c>* first tuple element is startcount of rebuildingstep</c>
<c>* second tuple element is endcount of rebuildingstep</c>
<l>if (ProcessingLoopcounter = 0)</l>
<c>    * init at startup</c>
<l>    Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorOut := {[1,ControlShiftregister_TriggerKill],[0,StepWidth_NumberOfFramesToRebuild]}</l>
<l>else</l>
<l>    if (ControlShiftregister_TriggerRebuild = 2)</l>
<c>        * if rebuild it set data</c>
<l>        Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorOut := {[1,ControlShiftregister_TriggerKill],[ProcessingLoopcounter , ProcessingLoopcounter + StepWidth_NumberOfFramesToRebuild]}</l>
<l>    else</l>
<c>        * if normal operation check if still active (count) or do nothing</c>
<l>        if (Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorIn.at(0)[0] = 1)</l>
<l>            SecondElementOfVector := Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorIn.at(1)</l>
<l>            if (SecondElementOfVector[1] = ProcessingLoopcounter)</l>
<c>                * reset to no rebuilding mode</c>
<l>                Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorOut := {[0,ControlShiftregister_TriggerKill],[-1 , -1]}</l>
<l>            else</l>
<c>                * is still in rebuilding mode</c>
<l>                Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorOut := Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorIn</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>        else</l>
<l>            Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorOut := {[0,ControlShiftregister_TriggerKill],[-1 , -1]}</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<l>endif</l>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="Shiftregister_RebuildCalc">
<parameters>
<parameter id="ControlShiftregister_TriggerKill"/>
<parameter id="ControlShiftregister_TriggerRebuild"/>
<parameter id="ProcessingLoopcounter"/>
<parameter id="Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorIn"/>
<parameter id="Shiftregister_RebuildDataVectorOut"/>
<parameter id="StepWidth_NumberOfFramesToRebuild"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="DisplayButtonsAndExpectUserInput">
<interface>
<io>
<par name="ImageOrig" base_type="iconic" dimension="0"/>
</io>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="InterfaceFromGuiFileAndPath" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
<oc>
<par name="ExternalIO_BtnPressed" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</oc>
</interface>
<body>
<l>global tuple Exitcondition</l>
<l>global tuple gGUILanguage</l>
<c>* init ouput´s</c>
<l>ImageOrigOut := ImageOrig</l>
<c></c>
<l>if (Exitcondition # 1)</l>
<l>    GenRegionsForButtons (ImageOrigOut, ButtonRectangles, WindowHandle, 24, 24, 400, 2)</l>
<l>    select_obj (ButtonRectangles, RectangleAgain, 1)</l>
<l>    select_obj (ButtonRectangles, RectangleOK, 2)</l>
<l>    dev_get_system ('engine_environment', EnvironmentIsHDevelop)</l>
<l>*     EnvironmentIsHDevelop := []</l>
<l>    if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop')</l>
<l>        dev_display (ImageOrig)</l>
<l>        dev_display (RectangleAgain)</l>
<l>        dev_display (RectangleOK)</l>
<l>        VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleAgain, WindowHandle, 'Farbe erneut lernen', 'black')</l>
<l>        VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleOK, WindowHandle, 'OK/weiter.', 'black')</l>
<l>        flush_buffer (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>    else</l>
<l>        * ButtonsIntervaceViaFile (InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath, 0, ['Cancel','Abbruch'], ['Reteach colour','Farbe erneut lernen'], ['OK/Next','OK/Weiter'], 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, ['Please decide if colour teach in is acceptable.','Bitte entscheiden ob Farbenlernen akzeptabel ist.'], 0, 0, 0, 0)</l>
<l>          ButtonsIntervaceViaFile (InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath, 0, ['Cancel'], ['Reteach colour'], ['OK/Next'], 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, ['Please decide if colour teach in is acceptable.'], 0, 0, 0, 0)</l>
<l>    endif</l>
<c>    </c>
<c>    </c>
<l>    RedrawGrafic := 1</l>
<l>    BtnPressed := []</l>
<l>    while (1) </l>
<l>        if (RedrawGrafic = 1)</l>
<l>            RedrawGrafic := 0</l>
<l>            dev_display (ImageOrig)</l>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop')</l>
<l>                dev_display (RectangleAgain)</l>
<l>                dev_display (RectangleOK)</l>
<l>                VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleAgain, WindowHandle, 'Farbe erneut lernen', 'black')</l>
<l>                VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleOK, WindowHandle, 'OK/weiter', 'black')</l>
<l>                flush_buffer (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>        endif </l>
<l>        Error:=[]</l>
<l>        if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop')</l>
<l>            dev_error_var (ErrorVar, 1)</l>
<l>            dev_set_check ('~give_error')</l>
<l>            get_mposition (WindowHandle, Row, Column, Button)</l>
<l>            Error := ErrorVar</l>
<l>            dev_set_check ('give_error')</l>
<l>        else   </l>
<l>*             UserIO_MonitorFile_GetBtnPress (InterfaceFromGuiFileAndPath, BtnPressed)</l>
<l>*             if (BtnPressed = [])</l>
<c>                * do something so output will not freeze</c>
<l>*                 set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'false')</l>
<l>*                 dev_display (ImageOrigOut)</l>
<l>*                 flush_buffer (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>*                 set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'true')</l>
<l>*                 wait_seconds(0.05)</l>
<l>*             endif</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        UserIO_MonitorFile_GetBtnPress (InterfaceFromGuiFileAndPath, BtnPressed)</l>
<l>        if (BtnPressed = [])</l>
<c>            * do something so output will not freeze</c>
<l>            set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'false')</l>
<l>            dev_display (ImageOrigOut)</l>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop')</l>
<l>                dev_display (RectangleAgain)</l>
<l>                dev_display (RectangleOK)</l>
<l>                VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleAgain, WindowHandle, 'Farbe erneut lernen', 'black')</l>
<l>                VisualizeInMiddleOfRegion_String (ImageOrigOut, RectangleOK, WindowHandle, 'OK/weiter', 'black')</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            flush_buffer (WindowHandle)</l>
<l>            set_window_param (WindowHandle, 'flush', 'true')</l>
<l>            wait_seconds(0.05)</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<c>        </c>
<l>        IsInside:=0</l>
<l>        if(Exitcondition = 1)</l>
<l>            break</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>        if (Error = 2 or BtnPressed # [])</l>
<l>            if (BtnPressed = 1)</l>
<l>                ExternalIO_BtnPressed:=1</l>
<l>                break  </l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop' and BtnPressed = [])</l>
<l>                test_region_point (RectangleAgain, Row, Column, IsInside)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            if (IsInside = 1 or BtnPressed = 2)</l>
<l>*                 Exitcondition := 1</l>
<l>                ExternalIO_BtnPressed:=2</l>
<l>                break</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<c>            * check if left is rectangle pressed</c>
<l>            if (EnvironmentIsHDevelop = 'HDevelop' and BtnPressed = [])</l>
<l>                test_region_point (RectangleOK, Row, Column, IsInside)</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>            if (IsInside = 1 or BtnPressed = 3)</l>
<l>                ExternalIO_BtnPressed:=3</l>
<l>                break</l>
<l>            endif</l>
<l>        endif</l>
<l>    endwhile</l>
<l>endif</l>
<c></c>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="DisplayButtonsAndExpectUserInput">
<parameters>
<parameter id="ExternalIO_BtnPressed"/>
<parameter id="ImageOrig"/>
<parameter id="InterfaceFromGuiFileAndPath"/>
<parameter id="InterfaceToGuiFileAndPath"/>
<parameter id="WindowHandle"/>
</parameters>
</docu>
</procedure>
<procedure name="plot_funct_1d">
<interface>
<ic>
<par name="WindowHandle" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Function" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="XLabel" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="YLabel" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="Color" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="GenParamNames" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
<par name="GenParamValues" base_type="ctrl" dimension="0"/>
</ic>
</interface>
<body>
<c>* This procedure plots a function in a coordinate system.</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Input parameters:</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Function: 1d function</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* XLabel: X axis label</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* XLabel: Y axis label</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* Color: Color of the plotted function</c>
<c>*        If [] is given, the currently set display color is used.</c>
<c>*        If 'none is given, the function is not plotted, but only</c>
<c>*        the coordinate axes as specified.</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* GenParamNames: Generic parameters to control the presentation</c>
<c>*                The parameters are evaluated from left to right.</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>*                Possible Values:</c>
<c>*    'axes_color': coordinate system color</c>
<c>*                  Default: 'white'</c>
<c>*                  If 'none' is given, no coordinate system is shown.</c>
<c>*    'style': Graph style</c>
<c>*             Possible values: 'line' (default), 'cross', 'filled'</c>
<c>*    'clip': Clip graph to coordinate system area</c>
<c>*            Possibile values: 'yes' (default), 'no'</c>
<c>*    'ticks': Control display of ticks on the axes</c>
<c>*             If 'min_max_origin' is given (default), ticks are shown</c>
<c>*             at the minimum and maximum values of the axes and at the</c>
<c>*             intercept point of x- and y-axis.</c>
<c>*             If 'none' is given, no ticks are shown.</c>
<c>*             If any number != 0 is given, it is interpreted as distance</c>
<c>*             between the ticks.</c>
<c>*    'ticks_x': Control display of ticks on x-axis only</c>
<c>*    'ticks_y': Control display of ticks on y-axis only</c>
<c>*    'grid': Control display of grid lines within the coordinate system</c>
<c>*            If 'min_max_origin' is given (default), grid lines are shown</c>
<c>*            at the minimum and maximum values of the axes.</c>
<c>*            If 'none' is given, no grid lines are shown.</c>
<c>*            If any number != 0 is given, it is interpreted as distance</c>
<c>*            between the grid lines.</c>
<c>*    'grid_x': Control display of grid lines for the x-axis only</c>
<c>*    'grid_y': Control display of grid lines for the y-axis only</c>
<c>*    'grid_color': Color of the grid (default: 'dim gray')</c>
<c>*    'margin': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area</c>
<c>*              to all four window borders.</c>
<c>*    'margin_left': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area</c>
<c>*                   to the left window border.</c>
<c>*    'margin_right': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area</c>
<c>*                    to the right window border.</c>
<c>*    'margin_top': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area</c>
<c>*                  to the upper window border.</c>
<c>*    'margin_bottom': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area</c>
<c>*                     to the lower window border.</c>
<c>*    'start_x': Lowest x value of the x axis</c>
<c>*               Default: min(XValues)</c>
<c>*    'end_x': Highest x value of the x axis</c>
<c>*             Default: max(XValues)</c>
<c>*    'start_y': Lowest y value of the x axis</c>
<c>*               Default: min(YValues)</c>
<c>*    'end_y': Highest y value of the x axis</c>
<c>*             Default: max(YValues)</c>
<c>*    'origin_x': X coordinate of the intercept point of x- and y-axis.</c>
<c>*                Default: same as start_x</c>
<c>*    'origin_y': Y coordinate of the intercept point of x- and y-axis.</c>
<c>*                Default: same as start_y</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* GenParamValues: Values of the generic parameters of GenericParamNames</c>
<c>* </c>
<c>* </c>
<l>funct_1d_to_pairs (Function, XValues, YValues)</l>
<l>plot_tuple (WindowHandle, XValues, YValues, XLabel, YLabel, Color, GenParamNames, GenParamValues)</l>
<l>return ()</l>
</body>
<docu id="plot_funct_1d">
<abstract lang="en_US">This procedure plots the function Function into the graphic window given in WindowHandle.
The axes of the coordinate system are labeled with XLabel and Ylabel.
The appearance of the output can further be adapted using generic parameters given in GenericParamNames and GenericParamValues.

In particular, following parameters can be set:

Function: A 1d function.

 XLabel: X axis label.

 XLabel: Y axis label.

 Color: Color of the plotted function.

        If [] is given, the currently set display color is used.
        If 'none' is given, the function is not plotted, but only
        the coordinate axes as specified.

 GenParamNames: Generic parameters to control the presentation.

                Possible Values:

    'axes_color': coordinate system color.
                  Default: 'white'
                  If 'none' is given, no coordinate system is shown. 

    'style': Graph style.
             Possible values: 'line' (default), 'cross', 'filled'

    'clip': Clip graph to coordinate system area.
            Possibile values: 'no' (default), 'yes''

    'ticks': Control display of ticks on the axes.
             If 'min_max_origin' is given (default), ticks are shown 
             at the minimum and maximum values of the axes and at the
             intercept point of x- and y-axis.
             If 'none' is given, no ticks are shown.
             If any number != 0 is given, it is interpreted as distance
             between the ticks.

    'ticks_x': Control display of ticks on x-axis only.

    'ticks_y': Control display of ticks on x-axis only.

    'grid': Control display of grid lines within the coordinate system.
            If 'min_max_origin' is given (default), grid lines are shown 
            at the minimum and maximum values of the axes.
            If 'none' is given, no grid lines are shown.
            If any number != 0 is given, it is interpreted as distance
            between the grid lines.

    'grid_x': Control display of grid lines for the x-axis only.

    'grid_y': Control display of grid lines for the y-axis only.

    'grid_color': Color of the grid (default: 'dim gray').

    'margin': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area
              to all four window borders.

    'margin_left': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area
                   to the left window border.

    'margin_right': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area
                    to the right window border.

    'margin_top': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area
                    to the upper window border.

    'margin_bottom'': The distance in pixels of the coordinate system area
                    to the lower window border.

    'start_x': Lowest x value of the x axis.
               Default: min(XValues)

    'end_x': Highest x value of the x axis.
             Default: max(XValues)

    'start_y': Lowest y value of the x axis.
               Default: min(YValues)

    'end_y': Highest y value of the x axis.
             Default: max(YValues)

    'origin_x': X coordinate of the intercept point of x- and y-axis.
                Default: same as start_x

    'origin_y': Y coordinate of the intercept point of x- and y-axis.
                Default: same as start_y

 GenParamValues: Values of the generic parameters of GenericParamNames.</abstract>
<alternatives>
<item>plot_tuple</item>
</alternatives>
<chapters lang="de_DE">
<item>Graphik</item>
<item>Ausgabe</item>
</chapters>
<chapters lang="en_US">
<item>Graphics</item>
<item>Output</item>
</chapters>
<example lang="en_US">dev_open_window (0, 0, 512, 512, 'black', WindowHandle)
X := [-rad(180): 0.01: rad(180)]
Y := sin(X)
create_funct_1d_pairs (X, Y, Function)
invert_funct_1d (Function, InverseFunction)
GenParamNames := []
GenParamValues := []
plot_funct_1d (WindowHandle, InverseFunction, 'x', 'sin^-1(x)', 'red', GenParamNames, GenParamValues)
</example>
<keywords lang="en_US">
<item>plot</item>
<item>function</item>
<item>display</item>
<item>graph</item>
<item>curve</item>
</keywords>
<library lang="en_US">MVTec Standard Procedures</library>
<predecessor>
<item>create_funct_1d_pairs</item>
<item>create_funct_1d_array</item>
<item>compose_funct_1d</item>
</predecessor>
<short lang="en_US"> This procedure plots tuples representing functions or curves in a coordinate system.</short>
<parameters>
<parameter id="Color">
<default_type>string</default_type>
<default_value>[]</default_value>
<description lang="en_US">Color of the function plot.</description>
<multivalue>optional</multivalue>
<sem_type>color</sem_type>
